   "applicability": "The transferred material is a health record under B-HRA 2 because it identifies one individual and concerns physical health and the provision of health care. However, B-HRA 3 limits Sections 4\u20138 to covered providers and service agents, and Section 9 to data hosts. Kestrel is a health care provider but does not bill a Region B-licensed health insurer electronically, and neither clinic is an insurer; therefore neither is a covered provider under B-HRA 2. Harrow receives and maintains the referral in its own clinical record for its own patient care, not on behalf of a covered provider, so it is not a service agent. The facts also say there is no external host and Harrow stores no records on behalf of anyone else, so neither clinic is a data host. The Records Access Act defines a computing provider as a person providing storage, hosting or computing services in Region B. On the facts, Harrow is using its own clinical referral portal for its clinical records, not providing a separate computing or hosting service, and no external computing provider is identified. Accordingly, no operative requirement in the read Region B provisions applies to this transfer or either clinic.",
